From: "qwen.ai[bot]" <qwenlm-intl@service.alibaba.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:04:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore: untrack committed .pyc caches and refresh stale G-5
 comment after PR #37

- Remove all 50 tracked *.pyc bytecode caches from the index (git rm
  --cached); they are regenerable build artifacts, already covered by
  the existing .gitignore rules (__pycache__/, *.pyc, .pytest_cache/),
  and are not needed at runtime.
- .gitignore is restored byte-for-byte to main: no changes in this PR.
- src/c5_runtime.py: replace the stale G-5 comment claiming the LIVE
  adapter masks a get_orders() error as open_orders = 0. After PR #37
  the exception propagates out of snapshot() and startup reconcile
  fails closed (STARTUP_RECONCILE_FAILED). The EXIT_UNVERIFIED freeze
  rule is unchanged: a single snapshot without open orders is still
  not proof of terminality of the previous SELL.
- No executable code changed; execution_adapter.py, C5 strategy,
  reconcile logic, ENTRY/risk logic, PaperExecutionAdapter and
  SimulatedBroker untouched.
